# WITHOUT THIS FILE THE IMAGE IS BUILT FROM THE DEVELOPER'S DISK (#21).
#
# The Dockerfile installs dependencies from package.json/package-lock.json and
# only then does `COPY . .`. With no ignore list that COPY includes the host's
# own node_modules, which lands ON TOP of the tree `npm install` just resolved
# from the lockfile. The image is then built against whatever the developer
# happened to have installed locally, not against the lockfile.
#
# That is not hypothetical. hugmesh-host-shell carries the same file because a
# corrected `overrides.@softarc/native-federation` (4.4.1, exporting
# isUnderAnyDir) still produced a build that failed with "does not provide an
# export named 'isUnderAnyDir'" -- a stale local 4.3.1 had overwritten it. It
# hid in the other direction too: the .stack-src build tree is a fresh clone
# with no node_modules, so the identical Dockerfile built fine THERE and broke
# on the developer's box. CI never sees it either, because a fresh checkout has
# no node_modules -- which is exactly what lets it survive.
#
# `tools/docker/check-context.mjs` (npm run docker:context, wired into pretest
# and prebuild) enumerates the build context under these rules and asserts both
# halves: that the junk below is OUT, and that every path the Dockerfile's COPY
# instructions and the in-image build actually read is still IN. Over-excluding
# here breaks the image just as surely as under-excluding does.
#
# NOTE ON PATTERN SCOPE: a .dockerignore pattern is matched against the WHOLE
# relative path, so a bare `node_modules` line excludes ONLY the root-level one.
# e2e/ has its own package.json and package-lock.json, so this repo really does
# grow a second node_modules -- hence `**/node_modules`, not `node_modules`.

# Installed/derived trees. Every one of these is regenerated inside the image.
**/node_modules
.angular
dist
out-tsc
coverage

# VCS, CI and editor metadata. Never read by the build; `.git` alone is tens of
# MB of context upload, and keeping .github out means editing a workflow does
# not invalidate the image cache.
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github
.gitlab-ci.yml
.vscode
.idea
**/*.swp

# Local env/secrets must never enter an image layer.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Test and report output.
test-results
playwright-report
**/*.log

# Docker's own files: editing the Dockerfile should not invalidate the context.
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
